					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-386109#post-1246235</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-386109/scp-755#post-1246235</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 31 Aug 2011 15:07:40 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>yellowrock</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>578929</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>It's interesting, but seems a bit overly verbose in some parts. I mean, it's essentially a guy that writes stuff, and when people see the stuff they get injured or killed somehow. The only really scary bit is the fact that some graffiti can be very public, and effect a large number of people, but that factor is, for me anyway, drowned out in the rest of the article.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-386109#post-1245761</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-386109/scp-755#post-1245761</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 31 Aug 2011 03:26:04 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>tunedtoadeadchannel</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>304457</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>This is not a piece of media. It's a person, and he doesn't kill anyone.</p> <p>Correlation does not equal causation, mrunimport- the whole point of the article is that the Foundation does not know whether the vandal is causing accidents or simply predicting them, and that there is evidence for both. That is why the vandal is the SCP here.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
